  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Green West Bank: promotion of green circular economy and green urban areas, energy efficiency, renewable energy, and sustainable waste management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pillar 2: Climate &amp; Environment GO: The Palestinian population makes use of the opportunities of a sustainable environment.  Intervention 4: Green West Bank SO4: The  conditions  of  the  Palestinian  ecosystems  and  their  population  are improved by reducing ecological footprint and GHGs emissions through the promotion  of  green  circular  economy  and  green  urban  areas,  focusing  on energy  efficiency,  renewable  energy,  and  sustainable waste management,  in the  region  of  Hebron  /  Bethlehem  and  Nablus  /  Tubas,  focusing  on  2  or  3 selected value chains. The Green West Bank project, as outlined in the Project Profile with COMP_ID: 6816 and INTE_ID: 4102, is a multisectoral initiative aimed at rural development in Palestine (SECT_NAME: Multisector. Rural development, TOP_SECT_NAME: Multisector. Rural development (43040)). Funded by the Belgian Development Agency (Enabel), this project&apos;s objective is to enhance the Palestinian population&apos;s ability to utilize sustainable environmental opportunities. The project focuses on improving ecosystem conditions and population well-being through various strategies, including promoting green circular economy and green urban areas to reduce ecological footprint and GHG emissions, focusing on energy efficiency, renewable energy, and sustainable waste management in Hebron/Bethlehem and Nablus/Tubas regions, and targeting 2 or 3 selected value chains. The project is overseen by the Consulate General of Belgium in Jerusalem, with Enabel&apos;s Resident Representative in Jerusalem representing the agency in Palestine. The project&apos;s budget and implementation details are specified in associated legal agreements between Belgium and Palestine.</narrative>
  </description>
